                <pb facs="0254" n="158" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg158"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 6 in No. 146 <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >bis.</hi>—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Moncrieff to Mr. Williamson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-04-25"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 25</date>.
                        (Received in Guatemala 2 p.m.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Arizona has sailed. Mr. James has shown
                    great tact and energy, and there will be no necessity for your presence
                    here.</p>
                <closer><signed>A. D. MONCRIEFF,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Agent Pacific Mail
                            Steamship Company.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
